#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37b088db-dca6-50cd-8af9-b057545eb87b" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Linear Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "33efc452-774d-50e9-94b5-215c9c117fec" :question/math-academy-id "e-13143" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{n \\in \\mathbb{N}: 5n - 2 \\leq 21 \\}$." :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\n5n - 2 \\leq 21\n$$\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $n{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5n - 2 & \\le 21 \\\\ 5n & \\le 23 \\\\ n & \\le \\frac{23}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe positive integer solutions of the inequality above are $1,2,3,4$. Therefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{1,2,3,4\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198087 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739c04ac-6d0c-5173-aa91-b5cc4dec8128" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Quadratic Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "88362b76-a41c-590b-9252-264c2bd4fcfe" :question/math-academy-id "e-13176" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}: x^2 - 9 \\lt 0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality $x^2 - 9 < 0$.\n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x{:}$\n$x^{2} - 9\\begin{vmatrix}< 0 \\\\ x^{2}\\end{vmatrix}< 9; \\sqrt{x^{2}} \\mid < \\sqrt{9}; \\mid x \\mid \\mid < 3; - 3 < x \\mid < 3$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm1,\\pm2$. Therefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198088 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "9518a07d-cf1c-51f1-9bac-7634caabc19a" :question/math-academy-id "e-13178" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A=\\{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}: \\mid k-1 \\mid \\leq 4 \\}$." :question/worked-solution "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality\n\n$$\n\\mid k-1 \\mid \\leq 4\n$$\n\nSo, we first need to solve for $k{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mid k - 1 \\mid \\le 4; - 4 \\le k - 1 \\le 4; - 3 \\le k \\le 5\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the above inequality are $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5$.\n\nTherefore, the given set can be written as\n\n$$\nA = \\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,4,5 \\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198089 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Trigonometric Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "21d6faa8-9340-5fad-8bf3-07ce92c449d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-13179" :question/problem "List the elements of the set $A = \\left\\{x\\in \\mathbb R \\::\\: \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0 \\right\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi x}{2}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{πx}{2} &= nπ \\\\\nx &= 2n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n\nSubstituting different values of $n$, we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\, \\pm 2,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\nA= \\{0,\\, \\pm 2,\\, \\pm 4,\\, \\pm 6,\\, \\ldots\\}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Absolute Value Equations and Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff821eae-25ee-5f75-bb04-76c3a7714c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0, ± 1, ± 2, ± 3, ± 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195133} {:answer/id #uuid "13648916-1ee7-54ac-a543-2